The [#4471 page](/kb/incidents/4471) calls every report one parser bug with one fix queued. The
reports describe three different problems, and only one of them is the parser. Each now has its
own ticket.

<Callout kind="warn">
The queued parser fix will not close #4471. The booking-v3 form and the one-day moves need their
own fixes.
</Callout>

## The split

<ProblemTable ticket={4471} />

## How each report was placed

1. Drop duplicate rows. The export comes in overlapping pages, so one id can appear twice.
2. Every report takes its tenant's cause from `causes.ts`: `hint` when it came through a
   booking-v3 form, `parser` otherwise. This is how the desk's own cause table counts.
3. A report the desk read as a one-day move (`desk-notes.json`) is also `timezone`. Its day and
   month are not swapped, so the parser cannot explain it. It stays in its tenant's count too.

The intake tag is not used. Intake guesses from the reporter's browser, and the cause depends on
the tenant.

## Why they ended up together

Triage merges on subject line alone ([decision 0001](/kb/decisions/0001-dedupe-by-subject)). All
three problems produce subjects like "Wrong day on the invite", so subject matching put them in
one ticket. The existing cause table shows the `hint` row with no ticket of its own and leaves
the one-day moves in a footnote under `parser`.

